    "title": "DONNA DONAHUE -",
    "text": "Trending\nDonna Jean Donohue, 91, of Marysville, OH, formerly of Steubenville, OH, died Thursday, September, 10, 2026, in Marysville.\nShe was born on December 18, 1934, in Steubenville, to the late Andrew and Hilda Donnelly.\nDonna was a 1952 graduate of Steubenville Catholic Central High School and a Catholic by faith. After graduation she held clerical positions at Jefferson County Technical Institute, Catholic Central High School and the Jefferson County Court House.\nIn addition to her parents, Donna was preceded in death by her husband Patrick Donohue.\nShe is survived by her children Michael (Dianna) Donohue of Marysville, Gary (Janie) Donohue of Steubenville, Kathy (Ed) Wolfram of Marysville, and Patrick (Jann) Donohue of Zelienople, PA, 11 grandchildren, Matthew (Jenny) Donohue, Michael (Leah) Donohue, Terry (Laurel) Donohue, Andrew (Brianne) Donohue, Jamey (Lauren) Donohue, Kaylie (Jarred) Kurucz, Daniel Wolfram, Joseph Wolfram, Christopher Carnivale, Amanda (Brock) Wagner, Lindsay (Logan) Hazard, and 11 great-grandchildren.\nA memorial mass will be celebrated by Fr. Kevin J. Kavanagh on Saturday, October 17, at 10:00 am at Our Lady of Lourdes Catholic Church in Marysville.",
    "summary": "She was born on December 18, 1934, in Steubenville, to the late Andrew and Hilda Donnelly. After graduation she held clerical positions at Jefferson County Technical Institute, Catholic Central High School and the Jefferson County Court House. In addition to her parents, Donna was preceded in death by her husband Patrick Donohue.",
